Package: confideR
Title: Protect Confidential Research Data When Using AI Coding Assistants
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("James", "Smith", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "james.a.smith@dpi.nsw.gov.au",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0000-0000-0000"))
Description: Provides tools to protect confidential research data during
    AI-assisted code development in ecological, environmental, fisheries,
    agricultural, and social science settings. Enforces a 'confidential mode'
    that clears AI API keys, blocks AI-adjacent R packages, and gates data
    loading. Audits the current IDE (RStudio, Positron, VS Code) for active
    AI features, including extension scanning and system process detection.
    Generates privacy-safe structural summaries ('fingerprints') from real
    datasets without exposing raw values. Simulates realistic survey datasets
    for safe use with AI coding assistants, supporting the 'develop on
    simulated data, run on real data' workflow.
